  "title": "AisleCatalog service",
  "agent_type": "developer",
  "description": "Add `CookbookApp/ShoppingLists/AisleCatalog.swift` \u2014 an `@Observable` (iOS 17) service that calls the existing `AisleConfigParser.parse(_:)` from CookbookCore when the configured folder URL is set or changes, caches the result, and exposes `aisles: [String]` (ordered as in `aisle.conf`, lowercase as written) and `isLoaded: Bool`. When `aisle.conf` is absent or fails to parse, `aisles` falls back to the canonical default order: produce, herbs, meat, seafood, dairy, eggs, cheese, bakery, pantry, canned, frozen, spices, pasta, rice, flours, oils, nuts, sauces, juices, world, baking, alko.",
  "status": "in_progress",
  "bead_type": "task",
  "parent_id": "B-bbc48bfa",
  "dependencies": [],
  "acceptance_criteria": [
    "`AisleCatalog` uses the `@Observable` macro (iOS 17+)",
    "`load(from folderURL: URL)` reads `<folderURL>/aisle.conf`, parses it with `AisleConfigParser.parse`, and caches the ordered aisles list",
    "`isLoaded` is false before first load and true after",
    "Calling `load` a second time (folder change) replaces the cached list",
    "Absent or unparseable `aisle.conf` falls back to the canonical default list",
    "Does not re-implement any parsing logic from `AisleConfigParser`"
  ],
